Root cause:
The bug was caused by the `seek_http` function returning `-1` when attempting to seek on non-seekable streams (where `source->len_ms == 0`). This return value was interpreted by the player as an error, leading it to incorrectly skip to the next item instead of handling the playback pause correctly.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (source->len_ms == 0)
    return -1;
```
Reason:
The `seek_http` function checks if the stream length is zero (indicating a non-seekable stream) and returns `-1`, which is interpreted as an error by the player. This causes the player to incorrectly skip to the next item instead of handling the pause correctly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (source->len_ms == 0)
    return 0;
```
Reason:
The patch changes the return value from `-1` to `0` when the stream is non-seekable. This indicates that the seek request is valid and does not signal an error, allowing the player to handle the playback pause correctly without skipping to the next item.


